{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>You shall diligently keep the commandments of YHWH your Elohim.</b> He says: it is forbidden for you to test Him; rather, you shall keep the commandments and believe as a general principle that He is righteous and upright, and all His deeds are in righteousness and justice. And the commandments that He gave you — they are benefit for the body, and in their fulfillment you do what is good and right in the eyes of YHWH, and He fixed a reward for this: למען ייטב לך, 'that it may be well with you.' For one who does a kindness with the king and does what is right in his eyes — there is no doubt that the king will repay him with goodness for doing what is right and good in his eyes. And if with a king of flesh and blood this is so, how much more so with the Righteous One of the world, who will repay with goodness and do good to those who perform His commandments after He commanded them thus, for He commanded only for the benefit of His creatures, as it is written (Deuteronomy 10): לטוב לך, 'for your good.'" "<b>And it is possible</b> to say that Scripture mentioned the three parts of the commandments: the rational, the traditional, and the statutes. מצות ה׳ — 'the commandments of YHWH' — are the mishpatim, which are the rational commandments; ועדותיו — 'and His testimonies' — are the traditional commandments, which serve as testimony to the divinity and to the creation of the world; וחקיו — 'and His statutes' — these are the statutes whose reason is not revealed. And after it mentioned that one must keep these three parts of the commandments and not test the Holy One, blessed be He, in any one of them, He gave warning about compromise — according to the Midrash — even in matters the Torah did not explicitly command; that is what it says: ועשית הישר והטוב, 'and you shall do what is right and good.' And because it is the cause of peace, He called it 'what is right and good in the eyes of YHWH.'"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:46:12.667280242Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}